  "description": "Jumeirah Capri Palace is in Anacapri, at Via Capodimonte 14, 80071 Anacapri, Italy. The hotel counts 49 rooms and 19 suites. Patricia Urquiola designed the newer suites. Jumeirah operates the house, and the page on jumeirah.com is the official site. The hotel's own map places it at 40.5529 north and 14.2138 east.\n\nL'Olivo holds two Michelin stars. Breakfast can be served there or in the suite, depending on the rate. Il Riccio is the beach club, and aMaRe is the restaurant named alongside it. A complimentary shuttle runs to Capri harbour and, when there is space, to Il Riccio and aMaRe. Sunbeds at Il Riccio are offered subject to availability.\n\nThe Capri Medical Spa is part of the hotel, set with the wellness rooms. The hotel writes about art and design as the other half of a stay: the suites carry Urquiola's plan, and the public rooms are hung as a small collection rather than as a lobby in the usual sense. The island is the view. Anacapri is the town, above the harbour, and the shuttle is how the hotel links the two.\n\nThe telephone printed for the hotel is +39 081 978 0111. The hotel email is jcpinfo@jumeirah.com, and reservations also use cpjreservations@jumeirah.com. The house is a resort on the island, with the rooms and the restaurants on one site and the beach club reached by the shuttle.\n\nThe stay suits days that stay in Anacapri, with dinner at L'Olivo and the beach club when a sunbed is free. Capri harbour is a shuttle ride away. The count of keys is the hotel's own: 49 rooms and 19 suites.\n\nRates that include breakfast name L'Olivo as the room where it is served. The same pages list the shuttle to the harbour as complimentary, and they list Il Riccio sunbeds as something the hotel can arrange when the beach club has space. Anacapri is the address. The harbour is the other end of that ride.",
